[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | grep hit | file:line | is it a rejection? |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |----------|-----------|--------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `#include <stdio.h>`  | `driver.c:26` | no — include directive |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `#include <stdlib.h>` | `driver.c:27` | no — include directive |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `if (line != NULL)`   | `driver.c:31` | **YES — the only rejection in the library** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `#ifndef DRIVER_H_`   | `driver.h:24` | no — include guard |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `#endif`              | `driver.h:29` | no — include guard |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the entire library has **exactly one** input-rejection site.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## What the C provably does NOT contain
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Establishing these absences matters as much as listing the one present check,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m because each absence is itself a behaviour the Rust must reproduce (namely: do
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m not reject, do not validate, do not abort):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no error-return macro (`RETURN_ERROR`, `CHECK`, `GOTO_FAIL`, …)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no `return <value>` of any kind — **every one of the five functions returns
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `void`**, so there is no error code or sentinel channel at all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no `return NULL` (no function returns a pointer)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no error `enum`, no status type, no `errno` read or write
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no `assert` / `static_assert` / `abort` / `exit`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no numeric range check, no `MIN`/`MAX` constant, no length or size parameter
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no `switch`, no `enum` parameter — therefore **no enum-valued argument can be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   passed across the FFI boundary at all**; the out-of-range-enum bug class is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   structurally impossible here (see row 5)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - no allocation, so no allocation-failure path
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `printf`'s own return value is discarded, so I/O failure is silently ignored
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (row 4)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Error-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `printLine` | `line == NULL` (literal null pointer) | `if (line != NULL)` is false → `printf` is **not** called → function returns normally, **zero bytes** written to stdout. No crash, no diagnostic, no status. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `printLine` | `line` points to a zero-length string (`""`, i.e. first byte is `\0`) — passes the null check but carries no payload | Accepted, **not** rejected. `printf("%s\n", "")` → exactly one byte, `"\n"`. Confirms the guard tests the *pointer*, not emptiness. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `printLine` | `line` contains `printf` conversion specifiers (`%s`, `%n`, `%d`, `%%`) | Accepted, **not** rejected and **not** interpreted. `line` is the *argument*, never the format string — the format is the fixed literal `"%s\n"`. Bytes are emitted verbatim. (A translation that used `printf(line)` or a Rust `format!`-style path would diverge here; this row exists to catch that.) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `printLine` | stdout is closed / unwritable (e.g. fd 1 closed, or a full device) | `printf` fails and returns negative; the C **discards the return value**, so `printLine` still returns normally. Failure is silently swallowed. Rust must also not panic, abort, or report. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | *(none)* | out-of-range `enum` value across the FFI boundary | **Not applicable — vacuously satisfied.** No function in this library takes an `enum`, an `int`, or in fact any parameter other than `printLine`'s single `const char *`. `bad`, `good`, and `driver` are all `void(void)`. There is no integer input whose value could fall outside a valid variant set. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `bad`, `good`, `driver` | any attempt to supply an invalid argument | **Structurally impossible.** All three take no parameters, so they have no input to reject and no rejection path. Each unconditionally executes its fixed sequence of `printLine` calls. Correct behaviour = never fail. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Rows 1–4 vs. the "generic boundaries" checklist
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The task asks to additionally cover null pointers, zero and oversized lengths,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and values one past a valid range, even when absent from the table:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **null pointer** → row 1 (the library's only real error path).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **zero length** → row 2.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **oversized length** → no length parameter exists; the analogue is an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   extremely long NUL-terminated buffer, covered as a *valid* input in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `CONFIGS.md` rows 7–9 (including the 4 KiB / `BUFSIZ` stdio-buffer boundary,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   where a divergence in buffering would surface).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **one past a valid range** → no range exists (no numeric parameter). The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   nearest boundary is the NUL terminator position itself; row 2 plus
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `CONFIGS.md` rows 4–6 pin that down, and the tests deliberately place a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   guard byte *after* the terminator to prove neither implementation reads past
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **out-of-range enum** → row 5, vacuous, justified above.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Status
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | row | test | result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-----|------|--------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `test_err_01_null_pointer` | PASS |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `test_err_02_empty_string` | PASS |
