[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axis derivation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options / modes / flags.** Grepping the public header and the source
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m for settable state:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -nE 'if |switch|#if|extern|static [^v]|global|_set|flag|mode|option' src/driver.c include/driver.h
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Result: **there are none.** The library has no configuration function, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m global variable, no `#ifdef`-selected behaviour, no init/teardown, and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m opaque context struct. `driver.h` declares a single symbol, `void driver(void)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only `if` in the whole library is `printLine`'s null check. So the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m option axis is a single point, and the configuration surface is spanned
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entirely by the remaining two axes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Input shapes the code is sensitive to.** `printLine` is the only function
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m with a parameter (`const char *`). Its body is `printf("%s\n", line)`, so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m shapes that can produce different behaviour are: pointer nullity (→ `ERRORS.md`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m row 1), string length (including the stdio buffer boundary, where flushing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m behaviour changes), and byte content (`%` conversion specifiers, embedded
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m newlines, embedded high/non-UTF-8 bytes — the last of which a naive
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `CStr::to_str()`-based translation would reject or mangle).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Full set of public entry points, lowest-level first.** From `nm -D`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | level | entry point | signature |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------|-------------|-----------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 0 (lowest — the output primitive) | `printLine` | `void printLine(const char *)` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 (calls level 0 once)            | `bad`       | `void bad(void)` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 (calls level 0, then a private helper that calls level 0) | `good` | `void good(void)` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 (composes levels 0 and 1 — six calls in a fixed order) | `driver` | `void driver(void)` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `printLine` is exported but **not** declared in `driver.h`; it is nonetheless a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m real public entry point (an external caller can `dlsym` it, which is exactly
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m what these tests do) and it is the lowest-level one, so it is exercised
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly rather than only through `driver`. Rows 1–10 drive level 0 directly;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m rows 11–13 drive levels 1–2; rows 14–16 cover cross-entry-point composition
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and process-level output state.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration-surface table
